  "decision_conditions": [
    "The application as submitted relates to the\r\nconversion of a family sized home within a restricted dwelling conversion zone.\r\nTherefore, one of the prerequisites is that the existing gross original\r\ninternal floorspace must measure more than 124sq.m. The existing internal floor\r\nspace including the ground floor extensions measures 111sq.m, due to this\r\nshortfall the principle of development in relation to Policy 20 (Housing in\r\nMultiple Occupation &amp; Conversions) of the emerging Local Plan could not be\r\nestablished.",
    "The proposed development contains a\r\ndisproportionate level of single occupancy dwellings without justification\r\ncontrary to the aims and objectives of Policy 15 of the emerging Local Plan.",
    "The proposed development provides a poor standard\r\nof accommodation for future occupiers in relation to flats 1 &amp; 4,\r\ncomprising of (i) combined kitchen, dining and living facilities that fails to\r\ncomply with minimum space standards, (ii) floor to ceiling height that fails to\r\ncomply with minimum space standards (iii) internal storage area that fails to\r\ncomply with minimum space standards, (iv) ineffective use of floor space, and\r\n(v) limited outlook. Therefore, the proposal would be contrary to Policy 56\r\n(Residential Space Standards) of the Emerging Local Plan, Policy D6 of The\r\nLondon Plan (2021) and London Plan Guidance – Housing Design Standards (June\r\n2023).",
    "In the absence of a Tree Survey (in line with\r\nBritish Standard 5837:2012 Trees in Relation to Design, Demolition and\r\nConstruction), to identify the impact of the development on the existing trees\r\non site and any other trees located within the vicinity of the development\r\nsite, along with the required protection and mitigation measures, a full\r\nassessment of the acceptability of the development and assurance of the\r\nprotection of local biodiversity could not be carried out, and therefore it\r\ncannot be confirmed that the development would be in compliance with ﻿Policy 80\r\nof the emerging Local Plan.",
    "The proposed development, fails to make adequate\r\nprovision for the storage of combined food &amp; garden waste contrary to\r\nPolicy 57 (Amenity) &amp; 93 (Waste Management) of the Emerging Local Plan and\r\nWaste &amp; Recycling Policy for Developers (2022).",
    "The proposed development, fails to make adequate\r\nprovision for the external secure storage of 7No. bicycles, contrary to Policy\r\nT5 of the London Plan, Policy 61&nbsp;and Appendix 1 – Parking standards of the\r\nemerging Local Plan and London Cycle Design Standards (2014).",
    "In the absence of a satisfactory Outline\r\nConstruction Logistic Plan, a full assessment&nbsp;of how the proposed\r\ndevelopment would be built or serviced without severely affecting the public\r\nhighway could not be made in line with Policies T7 of the London Plan (2021)\r\nand Policy 65 of the emerging Local Plan.",
    "The applicant failed to enter into a s106 agreement\r\nand therefore not in compliance with Policy 94 (Infrastructure and Developer\r\nContributions) of the Emerging Local Pan (figures applicable at the time of the\r\nassessment of the application):Car Free Development - the development is to be\r\nclassified as car-free and residents will not be eligible for parking permits.A condition survey of the adjoining\r\ncarriageway/footway on Forest Drive West covering a 10 metre dimension,\r\nincluding a site plan showing the where the photos were taken on the public\r\nhighway. Financial contribution of £2,508.00 towards the Epping Forest SAMA S106 contribution of £250 is requested toward CLP\r\nmonitoring.A S106 contribution of £3,000 is requested toward\r\nimproving walking and cycling facilities within the sites vicinity which will\r\ndirectly benefit future residents of the site.S278 agreement to remove the 2 dropped kerbs and\r\nreinstate the footway to current standards.Financial contribution of 5% for s106 monitoring\r\nfees."
  ],
